  "handbook/annex/p15/measure-extension.tex line 296 (readonly host) still disposes of the upper end with 'The upper-end proof is the reversed argument', and lines 381-392 still give the short truncation sketch. The full argument now lives only in the new owned lemma (owned annex lines 12-136), and nothing in the original proof points to it. A forward reference after routing would help.",
  "handbook/annex/p15/measure-extension.tex lines 512-516 (readonly host) still derive equality of laws and uniqueness from thm:p15-cdf-laws, whose statement covers real random variables only. The owned theorem thm:p15-w02c-p15-003-ray-laws supplies the missing identification, but the original proof does not cite it.",
  "The owned files' toc tag lists 158.1,158.2,158.5,158.8, but the new chapter holds only measure-extension material (158.1/158.2). The 158.5 gap was closed in the editable host, and nothing for 158.8 is in the new chapter.",
  "handbook/annex/p15/density-and-product-exercises.tex lines 307-309: the claim that mu is the half-and-half mixture of the laws with first coordinate fixed at zero or one (so mu >= nu/2) is asserted, not checked on cylinders. It is terse, but the argument is present."
